Bulgaria Explaues First Inflation Values For 8 Months
Monthly infflation in Bulgaria was 1 per cent, according to national statistics.
Although this is the highest value seen for years (since June 2012), last year, after a positive value of 0.2%, it has been seen above zero since October.
Average annual inflation measured by CPI for the last 12 months (August 2015 - July 2016), compared to the previous 12 months (August 2014 - July 2015) was 0,8%.
The consumer price index in July 2016 amounted to 100.0% compared to June 2016, meaning monthly inflation at 1.0%.
The inflation rate since the beginning of the year (July 2016 to December 2015 comparison) difference was -0.2%, and the monthly inflation difference between July 2016 and July 2015 was -0.2%.
Compared with the previous month in July 2016, a price increase was observed in the following consumer product groups: Food and non-alcoholic beverages (1.7%), transportation (0.8%), entertainment and culture (6.3%), restaurants and hotels (1.2%), various goods and services (0.3%).
Prices have decreased in clothing and shoes (2.2%), furniture, home equipment and routine maintenance (0.5%) and health (0.1%).
Alcoholic beverages and tobacco products, housing, water, electricity, gas and other fuel; prices in communication and training groups remained at the same level.
