Trading between Russia and Iran rose to 71% - RT Business
According to Levan Dzhagaryan, Russia's ambassador to Iran, the abolition sanctions and the trade turnover between Moscow and Tehran increased by 70.9 per cent year-on-year.
Since international sanctions imposed against Iran have been abolished, the interest of Russian companies doing business in the country has greatly increased, he said.
While new companies are preparing to gain access to the market, Russian companies maintain existing ties with Iran.
Of course, the further increase in commerce is one of the main priorities of our bilateral co-operation with Iran," Dzhagaryan said.
During the first five months of 2016, trade turnover between Russia and Iran increased by up to 70.9 per cent and reached US$856 million compared to the same period.
In particular, Russia's exports to Iran increased by 91.5 percent and reached 697 million dollars.
Russia's imports from Iran increased by 16 per cent to $158m.
This increase in striving was achieved with consumable materials for machinery, ground vehicles and weapons."
At the same time, Dzhagaryan expects a record number of Iranian tourists to come to Russia this year.
Last year, Russia's diplomatic representation in Iran gave Iranian citizens a 35,000-documentary visa, mostly for travel.
In addition, Iran was among the top 20 countries in the number of tourists visiting Russia for the first time.
We can say that the Iranian tourist record, which visited Russia last year, will be broken," he said.
At the same same time, relatively fewer Russians visit Iran, this is a matter that the envoy hopes to change.
