New faucet treatment: Trifocal Lenses
After cataract treatment, patients do not naturally want to use glasses.
In order to solve this problem in our patients, multi-focused lenses have already been used for many years.
With trifocal lenses that have been started to be used in recent times, it has taken a step further than the success of the treatment in this area.
The difference between trifocal lenses from other lenses not only far or close distance, but also at the distances defined as an intermittenuate distance is the ability to provide a clear visibility.
Treatment of distant, close or intermediate distance visual impairments
Intermittent distance in visual impairments represents a point that we use very often in our daily lives.
As an example, the instrumental panel of the cars, the portable computers we keep in our lap, or the distance we define as 60-70 cm arm size is the intermediate distance.
By recognizing the intermediary distance of trifocal lenses, our patients don't need to use eyeglasses in any way whether they don't notice.
Another advantage provided by trifocal lenses is to reduce night complaints.
Ophthalmology Specialist Associate Professor Volkan Hürmeriç "There is no difference in trifocal lens therapy for every distance vision treatment than normal cataract treatment."
Our hypofollological patients will easily get eye health with a 7 to 10-minute procedure.
And the next day, our patients can go back to their normal lives.
It's an operation that improves the quality of life especially for people who drive a car, have a lot of computer utilization, who love to read and lead a more active life.
You can also contact an ophthalmologist to find out if this procedure, which can be administered to every patient who has reached the age of 18.
